From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SheepyLord <37598021+SheepyLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 15:11:24 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Translate the Remix menus' 98 new texts (zh-CN, zh-TW, ja,
 ko, fr, ru)

The upstream merge of 2026-11-14 (20e3553eb) brought menu text the catalogs did not have: the
water simulation and its sludge, the dissolve of alpha-blended draws, colour inversion, the eye's
iris depth scale and limbal ring, the particles' spawn distribution and RTXDI's sparse neighbour
candidates. The build checks the .po files only against remix.pot, which had not been regenerated,
so it passed, and players of the six languages saw these texts in English.

update_strings.py regenerates remix.pot (3,452 messages) and merges it into every catalog: the 98
new texts are translated in all six languages, keeping to each language's glossary; the 16 to 18
entries whose English left the sources move to the end as obsolete #~ entries, and the other
entries' references move to their current lines. Each glossary gains the terms this batch settled
(the water's sludge, ripples, wind waves, swell, gusts and droplet rings, the dissolve and its
ramp, the limbal ring, the colour inversion's negative). update_strings.py --check passes, embed.py
reports 3452/3452 for every language (the fonts have every character used), and test_embed.py
passes. The translations are agent-written.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
