-#: src/dxvk/imgui/dxvk_imgui.cpp:3448
-#, c-format
-msgid ""
-"In D3D9, every draw call comes with its own fog settings. In Remix pathtracing, all rays need to use the same fog setting. So Remix will choose the earliest valid non-sky fog to use.\n"
-"\n"
-"In some games, fog can be used to indicate the player is inside some translucent medium, like being underwater.  In path tracing this is better represented as starting inside a translucent material.  To support this, you can copy one or more of the fog hashes listed below, and specify a translucent replacement material in your mod.usda.\n"
-"\n"
-"This replacement material should share transmittance and ior properties with your water material, but does not need any textures set.\n"
-"\n"
-"Replacing a given fog state with a translucent material will disable that fog."
-msgstr ""
-"在 D3D9 中，每個繪製呼叫都有各自的霧設定。在 Remix 路徑追蹤中，所有光線都必須使用相同的霧設定，因此 Remix 會選用最早出現的有效非天空霧。\n"
-"\n"
-"在某些遊戲中，霧可用來表示玩家位於某種半透明介質中，例如在水下。在路徑追蹤中，這更適合表現為從半透明材質內部開始。為此，您可以複製下方列出的一或多個霧雜湊，並在 mod.usda 中指定半透明替換材質。\n"
-"\n"
-"此替換材質的透射率與 ior 屬性應與您的水面材質相同，但不需要設定任何紋理。\n"
-"\n"
-"以半透明材質替換某個霧狀態後，該霧就會停用。"
